  "body": "**What's missing.** The browser build (#1103, #31) is served at `https://neotech.github.io/Camcraft/app/`. `release.yml` builds it, and a failed wasm build only leaves the \"not part of this copy\" page plus a warning. Nothing checks afterwards that the published page loads and starts: a page that serves HTTP 200 but whose module fails to instantiate, or a site-only redeploy (#3276/#3313) that drops the `wasm-app` artifact, would go unseen. Today (2026-11-24) `/app/` returns 200 with the loader page; whether the shell starts was not checked.\n\n**Proposal:** a daily check (on a collaborator machine or wopr's fast lane, no Actions minutes) that opens `/app/` in a headless browser (Playwright or Chrome headless), waits for the status line the shell writes its start-up state into, and reports:\n- the page and its module, wasm and shim files load (no 404s);\n- the shell reaches its ready state within a time limit, with no console error;\n- the version it reports matches the newest published tag (or the site branch's).\nA failure becomes an issue (`P3`: the published app does not start; a workaround is the desktop build).\n\n**Done means:** a daily job reports PASS/FAIL for `/app/` with the version it saw, and a broken browser build is reported within a day of the deploy.\n\nRelated: #3835 (release smoke test of the downloadable files).\n",
